You don't need gold.  You can lower your AC much further by sacrifice.
You just need to make a whole lot of sacrifices.  And it helps
immensely
to do it before you're crowned.

One admittedly abusive trick I have used, together with sacrificing
black puddings (hardly a "sacrifice"), is to manage luck.

#offer just to "reconciliation".  Drop the luckstone.  Then do
something that will lower your luck by 1.  Then #pray.  The chances are
much better that you'll get a point of protection.  You can get your
naked AC down to -127 or -128 this way.  You can get less spectacular
numbers without really spending all that much time doing it,
particularly if you can avoid being crowned.

Because of this exploit, I consider an altar near the sokoban entrance
with a sink on the same level to be too tempting to pass up.  Maybe
better than finding a wand of wishing on the first square.  I'm totally
serious.


